 "intro_text": "A book rhyme is a short poem or rhyme that was formerly printed inside the front of a book or on the flyleaf to discourage theft (similar to a book curse) or to indicate ownership.\nBook rhymes were fairly common in the United States during the 18th and 19th centuries, but the printing of bookplates pushed them out of use.",
